  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Raising awareness of the populations of the Cacheu and Oio regions (Guinea-Bissau) for climate change adaptation.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to raise awareness about climate change adaptation in the Cacheu and Oio regions of Guinea-Bissau. With a focus on vulnerable coastal communities, the project will enhance the knowledge of over 220,000 people, addressing the threats posed by climate change. The intervention includes community engagement through awareness campaigns, training local trainers, and setting up permanent exhibitions in public schools. Additionally, it will use local resources like community radio and educational institutions, such as the Bachil Teacher Training College (BTTC), to maximize outreach. By empowering local populations and enhancing climate change education, the project will contribute to long-term resilience and adaptation, ultimately addressing poverty and instability exacerbated by environmental challenges.</narrative>
  </description>
